  "name": "Furry Retreat",
  "shortName": null,
  "description": "Furry Retreat is an annual furry camp-out in Oklahoma, first held October 23 to 25, 2015, at Knight's Rest Retreat in Bristow. It was created by former Oklacon volunteers and attendees after that convention was cancelled, and since 2022 it has been held at Robbers Cave State Park. It is an event rather than a convention: there are no accommodations beyond space to pitch a tent and no scheduled panels, so a small core of staff and the attendees create a commune-like atmosphere with spur-of-the-moment events such as fishing, a gaming tent, a rave, fireworks and target practice. Early editions drew between 32 and 50 campers.",
